{
  "note": "When a folder-bound document's archive is written (ticket 26/09/30/NON-DESTRUCTIVE-HISTORY-EDITING design §22.22): the folder holds the document whenever this replica's log holds events the folder's archive lacks. Each case is the events one bound document sees, in order, and `writes` names the events (by index) at which an archive write starts. `publish`: the program published a batch. `absent`: the bind's first folder read found no archive. `foldStart`/`foldEnd`: a batch another transport delivered is being folded and settles (`ok` false: refused, nothing changed). `merge`: a folder read-back was merged, `ahead` events of this replica are not in the archive. `writeEnd`: the write in flight settles (`ok` false: it failed). Writes are single-flight with one trailing write; folds in flight are one write when they drain. Every shell's persistence reaches exactly these writes.",
